GitHub Actions with AWS

Today I learned how GitHub Actions integrates with AWS to automate cloud deployments securely.

🔹 AWS Credentials
GitHub Actions uses AWS credentials to:
Authenticate with AWS services
Access required resources
Perform deployments
Credentials are stored securely as secrets.

🔹 Deploy to EC2 / ECS
Workflows can:
Deploy applications to EC2 instances
Push container images to ECS
Automate release pipelines
This enables end-to-end cloud automation.

🔹 Secure Authentication
Best practices include:
Using IAM roles
Least privilege access
Avoid hardcoded keys
Security is critical in cloud CI/CD.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
CI meets cloud.
 Automation deploys faster.
 Security protects access.
